Path('VERSION-6-NOTES.txt').write_text("A Day To Keep 6.0\nExpanded journal-writing mode uses native IME visibility/insets. With the keyboard open,\nthe Home header stays visible; the date, navigation and reflection prompt are hidden;\nthe editor expands below the header. The export footer stays at its original window\nposition behind the keyboard (temporarily invisible), not above it. Closing the keyboard\nrestores the normal journal layout. Floating keyboards may cover content without\nreporting a bottom inset, so the editor still enters writing mode but cannot reserve\nspace for an arbitrary floating window.\n\nAdded shadow gutters, equal/gapped journal navigation, four compact calendar mode\ncontrols including an eraser, and 56dp month arrows with larger symbols in every calendar.\nHome panels and full-page backgrounds use seeded scattered artwork and periodic motion:\ntranslation, rotation and scale all complete integer cycles per 48 seconds. Theme selection\nreturns Home. Four appended themes preserve all 15 existing theme indices (19 total).\n\nWidget: A Day To Keep in the launcher Widgets list. Shows the current theme character,\ntoday's due-task count and completion bar. Tap opens Home. App changes trigger a debounced\nrefresh. Date/time broadcasts and Android's periodic widget update refresh it while the\napp is closed; Android may delay background updates. No exact-midnight alarm is claimed.\nThe widget artwork is a still image, not an animation. It uses the same mascot renderer.\nEmpty due-task lists display 'No tasks scheduled today' with an empty progress bar.\n\nSigning key/application ID unchanged; versionCode 6. Save a manual backup before installing\nOVER the current app. No uninstall needed. Existing interval rules, PDF attachments,\nexports, restore, sounds and settings remain in place. Keep source ZIPs private.\n\nValidation: generated Python/XML and Java lexical structure are checked; GitHub still\nperforms actual compilation and emulator execution. Pixel 11 Pro keyboard behaviour,\nshadow appearance, animation timing and real launcher widget placement need on-device testing.\n",encoding='utf-8')

